{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"felicific-blueribbon-kitty","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Summary\n\n`infra/gerrit/feature-branch-inventory.sh:81` decides whether a feature branch has landed with:\n\n```sh\nif git merge-base --is-ancestor \"$rev\" \"$main_sha\" 2>/dev/null; then\n    state=\"MERGED-BACK\"\nelse\n    state=\"ABANDONED?\"   # not in main's history — either in-flight or truly abandoned\nfi\n```\n\n`main` is **Rebase-If-Necessary**, so Gerrit rebases server-side on submit and the merged commit carries a **different sha** from the branch tip. `is-ancestor` on the pre-rebase tip then returns non-zero and a fully-merged branch is labelled `ABANDONED?`.\n\n## Reproduced on live data (not reasoned)\n\nRun 2026-09-05 against `origin/main = 4c9940348148`, comparing the script's predicate against a Change-Id lookup:\n\n```\nfeature/grounding-t2            MERGED-BACK  tip=709a46e9dbda  ahead=0  change_id_in_main=YES (709a46e9dbda)\nfeature/idea-status             MERGED-BACK  tip=6a28e9a5a6d7  ahead=0  change_id_in_main=YES (6a28e9a5a6d7)\nfeature/llm-provider-seam       MERGED-BACK  tip=5f00bf5253ee  ahead=0  change_id_in_main=YES (5f00bf5253ee)\nfeature/oss-readiness           MERGED-BACK  tip=c4c172914825  ahead=0  change_id_in_main=YES (c4c172914825)\nfeature/s1-windows-sweep-probe  ABANDONED?   tip=9c3c5ba2ea21  ahead=1  change_id_in_main=YES (2e131f2071a0)\n```\n\n**`feature/s1-windows-sweep-probe` is the specimen.** Its tip's `Change-Id` is present in `main` as `2e131f2071a0` (\"Make the Windows exclusive-leg tests runnable\") — the work fully landed — yet the inventory reports `ABANDONED?`. The four branches that label correctly simply were not rebased on submit, which is why the defect is intermittent rather than total.\n\n## Severity — deliberately p3, and why\n\nThe error direction is **conservative**. `is-ancestor` under-reports merges; it cannot report an unmerged branch as merged, so nothing here can mark live work safe to delete. Further, `--delete` is gated on **age** (`CAP_DAYS`) plus owner confirmation and does NOT consult `state` at all, so the mislabel does not gate any destructive action.\n\nThe real cost is misdirection: an operator or agent reading `ABANDONED?` for work that already landed may believe the work was lost and attempt to preserve or re-land it — wasted effort, and a duplicate-landing risk. There is a secondary observation worth recording: the computed `state` currently has no effect on the only destructive path, so the check informs a human and nothing else.\n\n## Suggested direction (not prescriptive)\n\nDetermine merged-ness by content/identity rather than by ancestry: look up the tip's `Change-Id` in `main`, or use `git cherry` / `git patch-id` to detect the rebased equivalent. Keep `is-ancestor` as the fast path and fall back when it says no. Distinguish three states rather than two — MERGED-BACK / MERGED-REBASED / NOT-IN-MAIN — so \"rebased and landed\" is not conflated with \"abandoned\".\n\n## Related, and NOT affected\n\nThe ticket close precheck is immune: it scans for a `rebar-ticket:` trailer on a reachable commit (`src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`), not for a specific sha, so a rebase-on-submit does not break it. Other `is-ancestor` uses reviewed and found sound in context: `infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh:123`, `infra/scripts/prepare_reclaim_backup.py:129/134` (tracker refs), and the test-suite uses (controlled shas).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 A RED test reproduces the mislabel: a branch whose tip is not an ancestor of main but whose Change-Id IS in main is currently reported `ABANDONED?`.\n- [ ] AC2 The detection distinguishes merged-via-rebase from genuinely-not-in-main, and `feature/s1-windows-sweep-probe` (or an equivalent fixture) reports as merged.\n- [ ] AC3 No regression in the four branches that already label correctly.\n- [ ] AC4 The relationship between `state` and `--delete` is made explicit — either `state` gates deletion, or the script says plainly that deletion is age-driven and `state` is advisory.\n\n## Constraints\n\nNever use `--force` or any gate bypass. `timeout` does not exist on this macOS host (exit 127) — bound with `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV'`. Terraform may be written and validated but NEVER applied. Do not touch the shared main checkout; do not `git stash` anywhere.","id":"3583-a119-db48-412d","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"feature-branch-inventory mislabels a rebased-on-submit merged branch as ABANDONED?"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788637241275139661,"uuid":"1ed60958-38d4-4123-9e01-3ff1ccead009"}